<<~ ahu slot=`#/pono-testability-merged-report`>>

! Pono testability: merged report (wave 1 codebase + wave 2 outside practice)

Kilo-Scout: Lares (Tasked Spirit), 2026-10-31. Repo untouched. Evidence files: `wave1.md` (measurements, file:line, commands), `wave2.md` (sources, fetched vs search-only). Claims marked ''testimony'' were not verified.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/tl-dr`>>

!! TL;DR

# The ratio runs ''1.41:1'' non-comment (204,871 test vs 145,127 source, TS/MJS), ''1.10:1'' raw, not 1.66. Weight sits in node (1.88), web (2.02), keyhive (1.60), tw5 (1.50); node+mesh+tw5 hold 74% of test LOC. Source is 39% comments, which is why the raw ratio understates. (wave1)
# The decisive seam is `prepareNodeBootOn`, ~2,840 lines (`open-node-vessel.ts:709-3546`, 164 closures, 49 `let`s). Test breadth follows from it: 1,032 `mkdtemp` in 389 files; 66 node suites in the serial heavy project. (wave1)
# ''New: the "Stryker activates no mutants" verdict has an upstream cause and a fix.'' Vitest 5 joined test names with `>`, Stryker 10.0.0 joined with a space, so mutants under `describe` reported Survived with 0 tests (issue #6262). v10.1.0/10.1.1 ("support vitest v5", 2026-10-23, eight days ago) fixes it. Re-probe 10.1.1 against the repo's vitest 5.0.3 before building a hand catalog further. (wave2 s1)
# Stryker's default is a ''sandbox copy'' (`inPlace: false`); the house's burn came from an inPlace run. Incremental mode and `mutate` ranges exist. Mutation score as the value measure is viable per package, as a list of surviving mutants (Google's practice), not as one number or an auto-delete rule: red-first controls kill no unique mutant by design. (wave2 s2, s4)
# The road rules the test re-cut AFTER the founding. Five items open seams without re-cutting and can run before; the stage-cut folds into the founding.

<<~/ahu>>

