<<~ ahu slot=`#/ranked-recommendations`>>

!! Ranked recommendations

Order tags: ''BEFORE'' = seam-opening, no re-cut, needs the operator's lift of `stable-founding-road.mem:268, 849` for the test-side parts; ''FOLDED'' = rides the founding refactor; ''AFTER'' = the re-cut itself.

# ''Re-probe Stryker 10.1.1 on vitest 5.0.3, in a throwaway worktree copy, one small package (memetic-frame or mempalace), sandbox mode.'' Output: does a mutant under `describe` get killed; per-test kill data; wall time; disk cost. Cost S. ''BEFORE.'' Sources: issue #6262 https://github.com/stryker-mutator/stryker-js/issues/6262 ; releases https://github.com/stryker-mutator/stryker-js/releases ; config docs https://stryker-mutator.io/docs/stryker-js/configuration/ . Fences: never `inPlace: true`; no dashboard reporter (web3-only); `df` first (WSL VHD law); sandbox must carry `dist/`.
# ''Eventful seams for the flake families'' (`LandedLedger.whenLanded`, store-ack on the unlock door, ready attribute + failure artifacts for the TW5 dropdown, event in browser two-tab test). Cost S each; 14+ owed sightings. Outside practice agrees that waits belong on a causal event, and DocHandle already exposes `whenReady` and a heads-changed event (https://automerge.org/automerge-repo/classes/_automerge_automerge-repo.DocHandle.html, search-level; not checked against alpha.5). Do not reach for `vi.useFakeTimers`: it patches the global clock, which the no-global-now law rejects; inject a clock and add the event. ''BEFORE''; red-first: the red forces the late event, the control forces the prompt one.
# ''Shared scratch helper via `test.extend`'' (temp dir, HOME, LAR_ROOT, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL as one fixture, with `onCleanup`) replacing hand-rolled `mkdtemp`. Source: https://vitest.dev/guide/test-context . Pilot on 20 node files, measure LOC drop, then codemod. Cost M. ''BEFORE.''
# ''Delete the 69 dead exports; produce a compiler-based list of test-only exports (wave 1: ~350 strict).'' Move survivors behind a `testing` subpath during module cuts. Cost S then M. ''BEFORE (dead + list), FOLDED (moves).''
# ''Characterization tests of the boot sequence around `prepareNodeBootOn` and `open-browser-vessel.ts`.'' Feathers' route: pin observable behavior before cutting (https://leaddev.com/technical-direction/how-refactor-legacy-systems-creating-application-seams, secondary). Cost M. ''BEFORE'' (tests only, no product change).
# ''Stage-cut `prepareNodeBootOn`'' into typed stages with a `Ports` record (fs, clock, env, network), thin shell composing them (functional core, imperative shell; https://kyle.au/notes/technology/development/functional-core-imperative-shell-pattern , secondary). Land whole, never as a half-injected interim ("Full models land early"). Cost L. ''FOLDED'' into the N/W/H trains.
# ''Inject homes and the operator hint'' (identity/storage/seal dirs, `readLocalOperatorHint`), retiring `withLarRoot`'s env mutation and the git-global leak. Cost M. ''FOLDED''; do rec 3 first.
# ''Mutation as an inspection list, per package, incremental.'' Run Stryker `perTest` + `--incremental` + `mutate` ranges (https://stryker-mutator.io/blog/announcing-incremental-mode/ , search-level) in CI on PRs, full run periodically; read surviving mutants, never the score alone (Google: raw score hard to act on; https://research.google/pubs/state-of-mutation-testing-at-google/ , search-level). Zero-kill tests become a review list, never an auto-delete, because controls and bug seeds kill nothing unique. Dynamic subsumption can cut mutant count (~52% runtime in Guimaraes et al., https://www.cin.ufpe.br/~damorim/publications/guimaraes-etal-icst2020.pdf , search-level). Cost M. ''AFTER'' for pruning; the pilot in rec 1 comes first.
# ''Extend the law pattern (fast-check + seeds + control + named mutants) to tw5 wiki-shore vectors and mesh face-gate/content-key-holder.'' Evidence in-house: 55 tests retired, 3 files removed, 5 faults found. Outside migration reports with numbers: none found. Keep the fixed seed. Cost M per package. ''AFTER'' (one pilot may ride beside).
# ''Per-project `isolate: false` and timed unit shards.'' Blocked until registries inject (74 module-level Maps/Sets) and `vi.stubEnv`/`stubGlobal` uses drop (https://vitest.dev/config/isolate.html , search-level). Vitest shards by file hash, not cost (https://main.vitest.dev/guide/improving-performance , search-level); extend `tools/e2e-shards.mjs`. Cost M. ''AFTER.''
# ''Witness consolidation'' (wrappers into one manifest; check overlap of `contract-witness.sh` 715 lines with `nexus-two-root`). Cost S-M. ''AFTER.''
# ''Report the ratio non-comment; track test runtime per claim, co-change churn and flake sightings per test beside it.'' The ratio is a bulk indicator; coverage/ratio targets mislead (https://www.thoughtworks.com/en-gb/insights/blog/are-test-coverage-metrics-overrated , https://blog.ploeh.dk/2015/11/16/code-coverage-is-a-useless-target-measure/ , search-level). No ratio norm found. Cost none. ''Now.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/where-outside-practice-conflicts-with-the-house`>>

!! Where outside practice conflicts with the house

* Stryker dashboard reporter: web2 service; use local reporters.
* `inPlace: true`: the burned mode; default sandbox copy only, in a throwaway worktree.
* Kill-set pruning vs red-first controls: controls kill no unique mutant; whitelist them.
* Fake timers vs no global now: inject a clock and add an event.
* Slice-by-slice refactor vs "Full models land early" and the founding road: land the stage-cut whole, inside the founding.
* Early test re-cut vs `stable-founding-road.mem:268, 849`: only recs 1-5 and 12 run early, with the operator's lift.
* Random property seeds vs repeatability: fixed seed stays.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/unverified`>>

!! Unverified

Where 1.66 came from; the prior scout's 233 method; the Stryker probe version that produced canon's claim; whether 10.1.1 passes this repo's suites; Automerge event semantics at 2.6.0-alpha.5; ratio norms; fast-check migration numbers; Stryker per-package monorepo recipe from upstream. Most outside claims above are search-summary level; only the Stryker pages (issue #6262, releases, runner package.json, config docs, vitest-runner docs, issue search) were read directly.

<<~/ahu>>

